ign=\"TOP\" width=\"4%\"> </td>\n<td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"5%\"><font color=\"#800000\" size=\"2\"><p align=\"JUSTIFY\">Total</p></font></td>\n<td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"6%\"> </td>\n<td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"5%\"> </td>\n<td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"4%\"> </td>\n<td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"6%\"> </td>\n<td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"4%\"> </td>\n<td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"6%\"> </td>\n<td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"4%\"> </td>\n<td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"6%\"> </td>\n<td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"4%\"> </td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n<font color=\"#800000\" size=\"4\">\n<p align=\"JUSTIFY\">A separate column on each side will be assigned to each account wherein\nthe daily gross receipt and gross charge will be entered from the personal ledger. Thus,\nthere will be but one single line in this register for the transactions of all personal\nledger accounts each day and its gross totals will give the figures to pass in to the\ncash-book.</p>\n<p align=\"JUSTIFY\">A page of foolscap has probably breadth enough for nine such accounts,\nif there be more than one page can accommodate, either the two sides may be separated into\ndifferent parts of the same volume, the same columns being carried across both pages, or\nmore than one register may be opened and the totals of the second, third, etc. carried\ninto separate columns of the first.</p>\n</font><div align=\"center\"><center>\n\n</center></div>"}